.\" OpenBSD-style concise man page
.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt DU 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm du
.Nd estimate file space usage
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm du
.Op Fl abchkLsSx
.Op Fl d Ar depth
.Op Fl Fl block-size Ns = Ns Ar SIZE
.Op Fl Fl apparent-size
.Op Fl Fl help
.Op Fl Fl version
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility displays the disk usage of each
.Ar file
argument and its subdirectories.
If no
.Ar file
is given, the current directory is used.
.Pp
Sizes are reported in 1024-byte blocks by default.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a , Fl Fl all
Write counts for all files, not just directories.
.It Fl b , Fl Fl bytes
Equivalent to
.Fl Fl apparent-size Fl Fl block-size Ns = Ns 1 .
.It Fl Fl block-size Ns = Ns Ar SIZE
Scale sizes by
.Ar SIZE
before printing.
.Ar SIZE
is an integer with an optional unit suffix:
.Ql K
(1024),
.Ql M
(1048576),
.Ql G
(1073741824),
.Ql T
(1099511627776).
SI suffixes
.Ql KB ,
.Ql MB ,
.Ql GB ,
.Ql TB
use powers of 1000.
.It Fl c , Fl Fl total
Produce a grand total.
.It Fl d Ar N , Fl Fl max-depth Ns = Ns Ar N
Print the total for a directory only if it is
.Ar N
or fewer levels below the command line argument.
.Fl d Ar 0
is equivalent to
.Fl s .
.It Fl h , Fl Fl human-readable
Print sizes in human readable format (e.g., 1K, 234M, 2G).
.It Fl k
Like
.Fl Fl block-size Ns = Ns 1K .
.It Fl L , Fl Fl dereference
Dereference all symbolic links.
.It Fl s , Fl Fl summarize
Display only a total for each argument.
.It Fl S , Fl Fl separate-dirs
For directories, do not include the size of subdirectories.
.It Fl x , Fl Fl one-file-system
Skip directories on different file systems.
.It Fl Fl apparent-size
Print apparent sizes rather than disk usage; although the apparent
size is usually smaller, it may be larger due to holes in sparse
files, internal fragmentation, or indirect blocks.
.It Fl Fl help
Display help and exit.
.It Fl Fl version
Output version information and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std du
.Sh EXAMPLES
Summarize disk usage of the current directory:
.Pp
.Dl "du -sh"
.Pp
Show disk usage of all files in a directory tree:
.Pp
.Dl "du -ah /var/log"
.Pp
Show disk usage to a maximum depth of 1:
.Pp
.Dl "du -d 1 /home"
.Pp
Show apparent sizes in bytes:
.Pp
.Dl "du -b file.txt"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr df 1 ,
.Xr ls 1 ,
.Xr stat 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility is compliant with the
.St -p1003.1-2008
specification.
.Pp
The
.Fl b , h , d , S , x ,
.Fl Fl apparent-size ,
and
.Fl Fl block-size
options are GNU extensions.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An "vibeutils implementation by Travis Cole"
